invariant: INV-17
file: quic.c
catches: quic_driver_test
reason: ch_quic_seal_close clears the level's write bit after its one
  seal and leaves the key bytes in the session, so a secret Handshake or
  1-RTT write key outlives the one packet it was kept for until
  ch_quic_close. test_close_after_failure requires the Initial
  connection ID and the Handshake send keys zero right after each seal.

--- old
    if (rc == CH_OK) {
        quic_wipe_write_keys(q, level);
    }
--- new
    if (rc == CH_OK) {
        q->levels_ready &= (uint8_t)~CH_QUIC_LEVEL_BIT(level, CH_KEY_WRITE);
    }
